  "environment": {
    "Overview": "Chinese garden architecture during the Song period provided private owners of gardens with a place to rest, enjoy leisure activities, host guests, and admire scenic beauty. While much information about them can be gleaned from sources such as paintings, poems, records, notes, and histories, most physical remains of them are now lost. Gardens such as Canglang Pavilion in Suzhou and Shen Garden in Shaoxing have been heavily remodeled since they were built in the Song period."
